# Project: DubMaster AI — Complete Windows-Based AI Video Dubbing Software

## 1. Project Overview

Build a complete, professional, Windows-based desktop application called **DubMaster AI**.

The application must allow users to upload or import a video, automatically detect its original spoken language, transcribe the speech, translate it into a selected target language, generate natural-sounding dubbed audio, and export a new video with the translated voice.

The application must work as a real desktop tool on Windows 10 and Windows 11.

This is not a website, not a static UI prototype, and not merely a command-line script. Build a fully functional desktop application with a modern graphical user interface, a reliable processing pipeline, real AI integrations, live progress reporting, and video export.

### Primary use case

For example:
- Import a video spoken in English.
- Automatically detect that its original language is English.
- Select Bengali as the target language.
- Transcribe the original speech.
- Translate the transcript from English to Bengali.
- Generate Bengali voice audio.
- Synchronize the Bengali voice with the original video.
- Export a new video containing Bengali dubbing.

The software must also support the reverse direction and other supported language combinations.

Examples:
- English → Bengali
- Bengali → English
- English → Hindi
- Hindi → Bengali
- Bengali → Hindi
- Chinese → Bengali
- Chinese → Hindi
- Hindi → English
- English → Chinese

Support additional languages whenever the selected speech recognition, translation, and text-to-speech engines support them.

All application interface text must be in English. Users must be able to dub videos into Bengali, Hindi, English, Chinese, and other supported languages.

