## 2. Recommended Technology Stack

Build the application using a maintainable desktop architecture.

### Desktop application
- Python 3.11 or another version supported by all selected AI libraries.
- PySide6 for the desktop graphical user interface.
- Qt Multimedia or an appropriate embedded media player for video preview.
- QThread, QThreadPool, or a proper background worker architecture for long-running tasks.
- SQLite for local project history, settings, and processing metadata.
- Pydantic for validated configuration and data structures.

### Video and audio processing
- FFmpeg and FFprobe for media inspection, audio extraction, audio conversion, synchronization, and final video rendering.
- MoviePy only if needed for a specific operation; prefer FFmpeg for reliable media processing.
- PyAV or another suitable media library if necessary.
- Temporary working directories for intermediate audio, subtitles, and generated voice tracks.

### AI speech recognition
Implement a pluggable speech recognition interface.

Preferred options:
- Faster-Whisper for local speech-to-text.
- Whisper-compatible models for language detection and transcription.
- Optional cloud speech recognition adapters when configured.

The application must identify the likely spoken language from the actual audio and display the detected language and confidence when the engine provides a reliable confidence estimate.

Do not infer the spoken language from the video filename.

### Translation
Create a translation service interface supporting:
- A configurable cloud translation API.
- An optional locally hosted translation model.
- Language-aware translation and preservation of meaning.
- Proper handling of Bengali, Hindi, English, Chinese, punctuation, and names.

Do not claim translation works offline unless an offline translation model has actually been installed and configured.

### Text-to-speech
Implement a provider-based text-to-speech system.

Possible integrations:
- A configurable cloud TTS provider with multilingual voices.
- An appropriate offline TTS engine.
- Additional providers through a common adapter interface.

For each provider, check whether the requested target language and selected voice are actually supported.

Allow users to select a voice when multiple compatible voices are available.

The architecture must support adding new AI providers without rewriting the entire application.

### Packaging
- PyInstaller for packaging the application.
- A Windows installer such as Inno Setup, if practical.
- A bundled or automatically provisioned FFmpeg executable, subject to licensing and redistribution requirements.

The final application must be runnable as a normal Windows desktop program, without requiring users to open a terminal for everyday operations.

