## 15. Offline and Online Modes

Support two clearly defined modes.

### Local Processing Mode
Use installed local models for supported tasks.

Depending on installed models, this mode may provide:
- Local speech recognition.
- Local translation.
- Local text-to-speech.
- Local FFmpeg rendering.
- Local project storage.

Clearly display which operations are available offline.

### Cloud-Assisted Mode
Use configured cloud services for supported operations.

Advantages may include:
- Higher-quality speech recognition.
- More natural voices.
- Faster translation.
- More language choices.

Show the selected provider and disclose when media or transcript content must be sent to an external service.

Never advertise full offline functionality if one or more required AI stages depend on a cloud API.

