## 17. Error Handling and Recovery

Implement robust handling for:
- Missing FFmpeg.
- Invalid video files.
- Missing audio streams.
- Speech recognition errors.
- Unsupported language combinations.
- Translation API failures.
- TTS provider failures.
- API quota limits.
- Network interruptions.
- Expired API credentials.
- Insufficient disk space.
- Out-of-memory errors.
- Interrupted rendering.
- Cancelled jobs.

Display useful, human-readable messages in the UI.

Provide a detailed local log file with timestamps and technical diagnostics, but never expose secrets.

Retry transient failures with bounded retries and sensible backoff.

Allow the user to retry failed segments instead of restarting the entire project.

Use atomic output handling so an incomplete render is not mistaken for a finished video.

